    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nOn successful owner creation, the pipeline now enqueues a welcome notification.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `NotifyOwnerWelcome.java`: a single-responsibility step that logs one line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the memberId (using `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier.of(owner)`, the same centralized identity source the existing audit steps use).\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notifyWelcome` step between `emitEvent` and `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors. It runs after `SaveOwner` (so `owner.getId()` is populated) and after `assignMemberId` (so the memberId exists).\n\nThis mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` / `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent` pattern rather than folding the logic into either of them, keeping each step focused. Full suite: `Tests run: 6, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, including the `coreEnqueuesWelcome` acceptance test that asserts a `NOTIFY` line carries both the id and memberId.",
